=head1 FUNCTIONS

=head2 SDL_GetPenDeviceType

  my $result = SDL_GetPenDeviceType($instance_id);

C: C<< SDL_PenDeviceType SDL_GetPenDeviceType(SDL_PenID instance_id) >>

Get the device type of the given pen.

Many platforms do not supply this information, so an app must always be prepared to get an SDL_PEN_DEVICE_TYPE_UNKNOWN result.

It is safe to call this function from any thread.

=over

=item instance_id - unsigned integer. the pen instance ID.

=back

Returns integer: the device type of the given pen, or SDL_PEN_DEVICE_TYPE_INVALID on failure; call SDL_GetError() for more information.

Since: This function is available since SDL 3.4.0.


